From fb201fb6c5a303693a421a6bf68aa92715d61a2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:18:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Dump: move onto the page structure (DumpPage +
 DumpPageContext)

- DumpScreen becomes DumpPage, the page's container, and provides
  DumpPageContext (capture, captureError, loadMore); useDumpPageContext
  throws outside it.
- DumpComposer reads capture and captureError from the context (2 props
  to 0); DumpFeed reads loadMore from it (4 props to 3).
- The route's {data} unwrapping and week key move into a pure adapter,
  toDumpPageProps(feed, totalCount, today) in src/utils/dump.ts, with unit
  tests; the route calls its two read actions, then the adapter.
- The Dump scenario keeps its fixtures in the read actions' raw shape and
  renders DumpPage through the same adapter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KCt6pMa91jhjUM2oez842a
